From b7c958d7c1eb1cb9b2be7b5ee4129fcd66cec978 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Osama Abdelkader <osama.abdelkader@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Mar 2026 16:16:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: kvm: fix vector context allocation leak

When the second kzalloc (host_context.vector.datap) fails in
kvm_riscv_vcpu_alloc_vector_context, the first allocation
(guest_context.vector.datap) is leaked. Free it before returning.

Fixes: 0f4b82579716 ("riscv: KVM: Add vector lazy save/restore support")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Signed-off-by: Osama Abdelkader <osama.abdelkader@gmail.com>
Reviewed-by: Andy Chiu <andybnac@gmail.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260316151612.13305-1-osama.abdelkader@gmail.com
Signed-off-by: Anup Patel <anup@brainfault.org>

diff --git a/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_vector.c b/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_vector.c
index 05f3cc2d8e31..5b6ad82d47be 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_vector.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/kvm/vcpu_vector.c
@@ -80,8 +80,11 @@ int kvm_riscv_vcpu_alloc_vector_context(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu)
 		return -ENOMEM;

 	vcpu->arch.host_context.vector.datap = kzalloc(riscv_v_vsize, GFP_KERNEL);
-	if (!vcpu->arch.host_context.vector.datap)
+	if (!vcpu->arch.host_context.vector.datap) {
+		kfree(vcpu->arch.guest_context.vector.datap);
+		vcpu->arch.guest_context.vector.datap = NULL;
 		return -ENOMEM;
+	}

 	return 0;
 }
-- 
2.34.1

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```
vcpu->arch.guest_context.vector.datap = kzalloc(riscv_v_vsize, GFP_KERNEL);
vcpu->arch.host_context.vector.datap = kzalloc(riscv_v_vsize, GFP_KERNEL);
if (!vcpu->arch.host_context.vector.datap)
    return -ENOMEM;
```
Reason:
The function first allocates memory for `guest_context.vector.datap`, then for `host_context.vector.datap`. If the second `kzalloc` fails, the function returns `-ENOMEM` without freeing the previously allocated memory for the guest context, causing a memory leak.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```
if (!vcpu->arch.host_context.vector.datap) {
    kfree(vcpu->arch.guest_context.vector.datap);
    vcpu->arch.guest_context.vector.datap = NULL;
    return -ENOMEM;
}
```
Reason:
The fix adds error handling to free the first allocation (`guest_context.vector.datap`) before returning when the second allocation fails. It also sets the freed pointer to `NULL` to avoid dangling references. This ensures no memory leak occurs on allocation failure.

